   "date": "2015-02-12T04:26:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Deploying shiny apps written as function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You should be able to take his code out of a function and turn it into single-file app:<div>  <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/single-file.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/single-file.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792363913551000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02MajvMtg8bEiAWFjLGVjM\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/single-file.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you want to keep the function, the app.R file could simply call the function at the end:</div><div><br></div><div>======================</div><div>myapp &lt;- function() {</div><div>  ...</div><div>  shinyApp(ui, server)</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div># Call myapp() so that app.R returns the shiny app object</div><div>myapp()</div><div>======================</div><div><br></div><div>-Winston</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Feb 10, 2015 at 5:38 PM, Michał Bojanowski <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">micha...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
